# Local secrets for `docker compose`. NOT tracked by git (see .gitignore).
#
# Copy to `.env` on the Docker endpoint and fill in values there:
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# How secrets flow (do not confuse the two mechanisms):
# - Compose interpolation `${VAR}` is resolved ON THE HOST when compose renders
#   the file (values come from the host shell or this .env file).
# - `env_file` entries are injected INTO THE CONTAINER as environment at
#   container start. provider keys below reach the app this way.
# - `inference.json` stores only the variable NAME (e.g. YT2WIKI_OPENAI_API_KEY);
#   the app reads the value from the container environment at request time.
#   `docker exec yt2wiki cat /data/config/inference.json` must never show a key.
#
# Example provider keys (leave empty / unset when unused):
YT2WIKI_OPENAI_API_KEY=
YT2WIKI_GEMMA_API_KEY=
YT2WIKI_LAN_KEY=

# Operator password for the browser login (first-run authentication).
# No default: with this empty, all browser mutations stay disabled.
# Set a strong value here (or in the Portainer stack variables), then restart.
# YT2WIKI_OPERATOR_PASSWORD=
